,title,link,text,language,family
0,Lachi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lachi_language,"The Lachi language is a Kra language spoken in Yunnan, China and in northern Vietnam.Weera Ostapirat[3] proposed three major subdivisions for the Lachi language. Northern (Chinese or Flowery Lachi). Central (White Lachi). Southern (Long Haired and Black Lachi).","Lachi, White",Kra-Dai
1,Kra–Dai languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kra–Dai_languages,"In 1942, Benedict placed three Kra languages (Gelao, Laqua (Qabiao), and Lachi) together with Hlai in a group that he called ""Kadai"", from ka, meaning ""person"" in Gelao and Laqua and dai, a form of a Hlai autonym. [10]","Lachi, White",Kra-Dai
2,Tai-Kadai - Max Planck Society,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Tai-Kadai.htm,"Western Kra: A'ou Gelao, Duoluo Gelao (White Gelao), Hagei Gelao, Qau Gelao, Green Gelao, Red Gelao, Lachi, White Lachi, Mulao Kam-Tai: Kam-Sui: † Ahom, Ai-Cham, Biao, Cao Miao, Chadong, Northern Dong, Southern Dong, Kang, Mak, Mulam, Maonan, Sui, T'en (Yanghuang) Lakkia: Lakkja, Lingao Tai: Unclassified: E, Kuan, Tay K h ang, Tai Pao, Tai Y o","Lachi, White",Kra-Dai
3,"Shakira, Burna Boy - Dai Dai (Official Video) - YouTubeKra–Dai languages - WikipediaLachi | Official Website - Music • Storytelling • FashionContext 27494: White Lachi (Source: Kra or Kadai languages ...Amaravati: Abode of Amritas",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fcnDmrtj6Sk,"(Playback ID: msqgVkT1WpjHuEzH) Music: https://songwhip.com/shakira/dai-daiLetra/Lyrics: Oe oe e oe Oe oe e oeYou knew from the day you were bornThat here in this place you belongYou been t... In 1942, Benedict placed three Kra languages (Gelao, Laqua (Qabiao), and Lachi) together with Hlai in a group that he called ""Kadai"", from ka, meaning ""person"" in Gelao and Laqua and dai, a form of a Hlai autonym. [10] Lachi advocates for Disability Inclusion in Music, Entertainment and Corporate America, from the Green Room to the Board Room - with creative inclusive-forward project, keynotes, consulting and brand partnerships. Kra or Kadai languages Jerold A. Edmondson. 2008. ""Kra or Kadai Languages."" In The Tai-Kadai Languages, edited by Anthony V. N. Diller et al. 653-671. Routledge. He split the Kra languages among two different branches, grouping Laha with Hlai rather than with Gelao and Lachi (Ostapirat's 'Western Kra'). I don't know how he would classify Paha (Ostapirat's 'Central Kra') and Buyang and Pubiao (Ostapirat's 'Eastern Kra'). Is Kra Dai a Chinese language? Outside China, the Kra–Dai languages are now classified as an independent family. In China, they are called Dong–Tai (侗台) or Zhuang–Dong (壮侗) languages and are generally included, along with the Hmong–Mien languages, in the Sino-Tibetan family. How many Kra Dai branches are there? Kra–Dai consists of at least five well-established branches, namely Kra, Kam–Sui, Tai, Be, and Hlai (Ostapirat 2005:109). Chinese linguists have also proposed a Kam–Tai group that includes Kam–Sui, Tai, and Be. Kra–Dai languages that are not securely classified and may constitute independent Kra–Dai branches include the following: Where did the Lachi come from? According to American linguist Jerold A. Edmondson, the Lachi of China are thought to have moved to their present location during the Qing Dynasty from places in Vietnam called Maibu 麥布, Maidu 麥督, and Maiha 麥哈. Other Lachis are also found scattered in Yanshan, Qiubei, Xichou, and Malipo counties. Is Kadai the same as Daic? ""Kadai"" is sometimes used to refer to the entire Kra–Dai family, including by Solnit (1988). Adding to the confusion, some other references [which?] restrict the usage of ""Kadai"" to only the Kra branch of the family. The name ""Daic"" is used by Roger Blench (2008).","Lachi, White",Kra-Dai
